  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fc730475ed18dc949b8c9fd8435ab43e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Floor3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  introLines: []
  casualLines:
  - I told you.... Now here we go again...
  - You see, you can never escape this unless you listen to me
  - But I know you too well, you will not.
  - Should I continue the story from last time.
  - Maybe then you will realise why you are here in the first place.
  - '"Something had happened, something A had forgotten. But the figures were patient.
    They did not attack. They only waited for recognition.'
  - "A began noticing changes each visit. Marks scratched into the walls, faint symbols
    drawn in the dust, the soft vibration of a melody no one else could hear. Every
    detail tugged at something buried in A\u2019s mind."
  - "They remembered suddenly, in flashes: a scream, a hand reaching, the wrong turn,
    a life they couldn\u2019t undo"
  - The hallway itself seemed to twist with the weight of what had happened.
  - 'A whispered the numbers scrawled in the dust, scratched into the walls: the
    sequence of that night'
  - "Slowly, painfully, the fragments of memory aligned. The truth, horrific and
    inescapable, settled in A\u2019s chest like stone."
  - "\u201CYou remember now,\u201D the silence seemed to whisper. \u201CYou cannot
    escape.\u201D"
  - A understood. The hallway, the figures, the endless repetition. They were not
    punishment. They were witnesses. Reminders. Guides.
  - The elevator opened again. The hallway stretched endlessly before A, dim and
    humming, the same sickly yellow lights flickering above. The figures were there,
    waiting.
  - "But A turned. Every time. They couldn\u2019t face it. They walked past the anomalies,
    through the same hallway, down the same endless loop. The numbers, the marks,
    the scratches, they all tried to reach them, to force acknowledgment."
  - "A\u2019s mind blurred, fragments of memory scratching at the edges. But they
    ignored it. They always ignored it."
  - The light never came. The elevator doors never truly opened. The sequence, the
    truth, hovered just beyond reach.
  - A would never stop. A would never confront them.
  - And so the hallway went on, endless, flickering, cold. The dead waited. The anomalies
    waited. And A walked, forever, avoiding the only thing that could set them free.
  - ..
